Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] esp32/inisetup: make a new filesystem over stale flash.

When the partition table leaves the filesystem out, the port puts it in
the flash after the last partition, so its start follows the size of the
app. Flashing an image with a smaller app over one with a larger app
moves the filesystem down onto flash that still holds the old firmware
(micropython-pydevices#185).

_boot.py then can't mount it, and check_bootsec() finds a first sector
that isn't blank. It calls fs_corrupted(), which prints a warning every
three seconds forever. _boot.py runs before mp_usbd_init(), so on a
board with a native USB console the port never appears and the warning
is never seen.

check_bootsec() now also looks for a filesystem: a FAT boot sector's
55 AA, or the "littlefs" name in the superblock of block 0 or block 1.
When neither is there, nothing on that flash is anyone's files, and it
makes a new filesystem. A filesystem that is there but won't mount still
goes to fs_corrupted() as before.

Based-on: micropython b70ae1aca (v1.30.0-preview-160)
---
--- a/ports/esp32/modules/inisetup.py
+++ b/ports/esp32/modules/inisetup.py
@@ -12,9 +12,22 @@
             break
     if empty:
         return True
+    if not holds_filesystem(buf):
+        # The filesystem's start moved, onto flash left over from an earlier, larger
+        # image. There are no files here to keep, so make a new filesystem.
+        print("No filesystem found where it starts now, so making a new one.")
+        return True
     fs_corrupted()
 
 
+def holds_filesystem(buf):
+    # A FAT boot sector ends in 55 AA; littlefs names itself in block 0 or block 1.
+    if buf[510:512] == b"\x55\xaa" or buf[8:16] == b"littlefs":
+        return True
+    bdev.readblocks(1, buf)
+    return buf[8:16] == b"littlefs"
+
+
 def fs_corrupted():
     import time
     import micropython
